```

Verify TrashBin exists in icons? I saw only person/camera grep. Let me not use TrashBin unless verified — I'll check quickly. Actually just include a check in the same command run as typecheck... better verify now to avoid a failed build cycle. I'll grep icons esm for TrashBin.

Form:

```tsx
interface ProfileFormState {
  name: string;
  email: string;
  language: string;
  timezone: string;
  twoFactorEnabled: boolean;
  notifyProductNews: boolean;
  notifySystemAlerts: boolean;
  notifyWeeklyDigest: boolean;
}
```

Avatar handled separately (avatarPreview URL + file).

Save: setSavedState snapshot; show saved message; Cancel: reset to snapshot.

Sections inside Card:
1. Основная информация (name, email)
2. Аватар
3. Региональные настройки (language, timezone)
4. Безопасность (2FA switch)
5. Email-уведомления (checkboxes)
Footer: buttons.

Actually simpler: one Card with all fields + footer inside. Section headers subheader-2 or subheader-3.

Field label helper:

```tsx
function Field({label, hint, children}: ...) {
  return (
    <Flex direction="column" gap={1}>
      <Text variant="body-2" color="secondary">{label}</Text> — hmm label usually primary body-2 medium. Use body-2.
      {children}
      {hint && <Text variant="caption-2" color="hint">{hint}</Text>}
    </Flex>
  );
}
```

Avatar upload:
```tsx
const fileInputRef = React.useRef<HTMLInputElement>(null);
const [avatarPreview, setAvatarPreview] = React.useState<string | null>(null);
const handleFileChange = (e: React.ChangeEvent<HTMLInputElement>) => {
  const file = e.target.files?.[0];
  if (!file) return;
  if (avatarPreview) URL.revokeObjectURL(avatarPreview);
  setAvatarPreview(URL.createObjectURL(file));
};
```
Cleanup on unmount with useEffect returning revoke.

Initials:
```ts
const initials = state.name.trim().split(/\s+/).map(p => p[0]).slice(0, 2).join('').toUpperCase() || '?';
```

Avatar render:
```tsx
{avatarPreview
  ? <Avatar imgUrl={avatarPreview} size="xl" withImageBorder />
  : <Avatar text={initials} size="xl" theme="brand" />}
```

Note: avatar preview isn't part of the snapshot reset... keep simple: cancel also clears preview? Snapshot includes avatarUrl: string | null. On cancel reset to snapshot avatarUrl. Track initial snapshot including avatar. Fine — include avatarUrl in state object, and revoke created URLs when replaced. Simpler: keep avatarUrl inside form state and snapshot together; revoke only the current preview when replaced with another object URL. Good enough; minor leak acceptable but let's revoke on replace and on unmount of latest.

Buttons:
```tsx
<Button view="action" size="l" onClick={handleSave}>Сохранить</Button>
<Button view="outlined" size="l" onClick={handleCancel}>Отмена</Button>
```

Email validation on save:
```ts
const emailValid = /^[^\s@]+@[^\s@]+\.[^\s@]+$/.test(state.email);
if (!emailValid) { setEmailError('Введите корректный email'); return; }
```
TextInput error prop: `errorMessage` + `validationState="invalid"`. TextInputProps has error?: string|boolean, errorMessage, validationState. Use `errorMessage={emailError}` and `validationState={emailError ? 'invalid' : undefined}`.

Saved message: `<Text variant="body-2" color="positive">Изменения сохранены</Text>` shown when justSaved, cleared on any change. 

Page container: 
```tsx
<Box spacing={{p: 6}} className="app">
  <Flex direction="column" gap={6} className="app__container">
```
App.css:
```css
.app {
  min-height: 100vh;
  background: var(--g-color-base-background);
}
.app__container {
  max-width: 720px;
  margin: 0 auto;
  width: 100%;
}
.app__hidden-input { display: none; }
```

Card: `<Card type="container" view="outlined" size="l">` — Card has own padding? Card size l padding. Box spacing inside anyway. Card extends BoxProps so spacing works: `spacing={{p: 5}}`.

Wait — BoxProps: does it include `spacing`? Traps say `Box spacing={{p: 4, mb: 3}}`. CardProps extends BoxProps so yes.

Select width: 'max' to fill.

For 2FA row: Flex justifyContent="space-between" alignItems="center": left = Text body-2 "Двухфакторная авторизация" + caption hint; right = Switch. Flex contract: switch flexShrink 0, text minWidth 0.

Notifications: Flex column gap={2} with 3 checkboxes.

Divider between sections? uikit has Divider component — saw it in list. Use `<Divider />`? It's fine to use; simple. Or just gaps. I'll use Flex column gap={6} with sections, maybe dividers for visual structure. Keep gaps only, simpler.

Language select content: for select options, `content` is ReactNode; strings fine.

Timezone select filterable with filterPlaceholder="Поиск по городу или UTC".

Now check TrashBin icon existence, then write files.

